  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The model's performance and utility are illustrated using a single case study in the Cape Floristic Region, without a comparative benchmark against other spatio-temporal modeling techniques.",
      "what": "The paper introduces the spatio-temporal generalized dissimilarity mixed model (stGDMM), extending previous spatial-only models to analyze beta diversity across both space and time. The model is demonstrated using Bray-Curtis dissimilarity metrics applied to a biodiversity dataset from the Cape Floristic Region in South Africa.",
      "why": "It provides a statistical framework to model ecological beta diversity over joint space-time pairs, enabling researchers to quantify how species composition changes dynamically across both geographic distance and temporal intervals simultaneously."
    }
